{
  "_doc": {
    "about": "Message HTML cleaning both clients must pass: web cleanMessageHtml (web/src/lib/sanitize.ts, DOMPurify) and Android cleanMessageHtml (android/core/.../mail/EmailHtml.kt, jsoup Safelist). They serialize differently, so cases check characteristics, not exact output.",
    "cidMissing": "Optional per case: content id → label for an inline image whose part couldn't be fetched (offline). Run cleanMessageHtml(html, cidUrls, cidMissing): an <img> with that cid and no data URL becomes a <span data-cid-missing> box whose text is the label; a cid in neither map just loses its src. `opensOnline` is the text both apps put after an unfetched part's name and size; `missingLabels` pin missingPartLabel(filename, size): the name when there is one, the size as attachments show it, then that text, joined by \" · \".",
    "check": "Run cleanMessageHtml(html, cidUrls) → { html, hasRemoteImages, colorSchemes }. hasRemoteImages and colorSchemes (the contents of `color-scheme` and `supported-color-schemes` meta tags, in order) must equal the fixture's. Normalize the output: '<br />' and '<br/>' → '<br>', whitespace between tags removed (/>\\s+</ → '><'), other whitespace runs → one space. Every `contains` string must appear in it as is; no `absent` string may appear in it, compared case-insensitively. Attribute checks name one attribute in double quotes, so attribute order and quoting style of the rest don't matter.",
    "edgeMargins": "A body's leading <p> gets margin-top:0 and its trailing <p> margin-bottom:0, appended to its style (with ';' when the style doesn't end in one). The edge is the first (last) child that is an element other than style, meta, link or title, skipping whitespace text and comments, looked for again inside div, center, section, article, main, header and footer; text there, or any other element, means no paragraph is trimmed on that side."
  },
